{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs3EHh1GbLKCDYWtAVUf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The constrained packages now skip the max-release-age filter. The unconstrained behaviour is unchanged. `tests/test_cooldown.py` passes (38 tests), including the two new ones.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/resolver.py`, `find_all_matching_from_provider()`**: if `max_age_cutoff` is set and `provider.constraints.get_constraint(req.name)` returns a constraint, the function logs at INFO `\"<name>: skipping age filter for constrained package (<N> candidate(s))\"` and keeps all candidates. Otherwise the existing filter and fallback run unchanged.\n- **Docstring**: the `max_age_cutoff` argument now says constrained packages are exempt.\n- **`tests/test_cooldown.py`**:\n  - `test_max_release_age_skips_constrained_package` pins `test-pkg==1.2.2` (older than a 5-day window) and expects `[\"1.2.2\"]` plus the new INFO message, with no \"keeping all\" warning.\n  - `test_max_release_age_filters_unconstrained_package` uses the same fixture with no pin and expects only `[\"2.0.0\"]`.\n  - I also added a `constraints` import to the module-level import block.\n- **`docs/how-tos/multiple-version-bootstrap.rst`**: one sentence under `--max-release-age` saying pinned packages are exempt. This wasn't in your list, so say if you'd rather drop it.\n\n**Choices I made**\n\n- The skip log only fires when `max_age_cutoff` is set. With no cutoff there's no age filter to skip, so the message would be misleading.\n- The check uses `provider.constraints`, which means any constraint on the name counts, not only `==` pins. That matches your \"a constraint is explicit user intent\" wording.\n\n**Not run:** `ruff` and `mypy` aren't installed in `.venv`, so I skipped the lint and type checks. I didn't install them, since that needs your approval. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,